      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the code. The original test has many unused imports and unused constants that clutter the file. The actual test method can also be made clearer by breaking the chained call into named steps. I'll write the improved version now.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports and constants, renames the formatter variable to `dayOfYearFormatter` for clarity, extracts the parsed result into a named `parsed` variable, and adds a brief comment explaining the `\"D\"` pattern — all while preserving the exact same method calls and expected outcomes as the original."
